the legalization of medicinal cannabis  in 2018 should have provided relief to  thousands like andrew who rely on it  but costly private prescriptions mean  access is still a major problem and the  fear of being found in possession of the  drug by police is still rife it started  with  feeling  we've we're finally here we're finally  being recognized  to to still being in this position i am  today where i'm still having to get my  medication  through  the route that i don't want to be going  through without it sounding too drastic  um  i don't think i would be here to be  honest with you if if i didn't have that  tool in my box  to be able to use and i know that sounds  drastic and it will sound drastic to a  lot of people but no that is the truth  after being arrested and having his  medication confiscated multiple times  andrew now carries a can card it has my  information on it's got my photograph on  it a type of id requiring medical  evidence from a gp which proves he's  eligible to use cannabis for health  reasons  since its rollout last year can card has  prevented nearly one and a half thousand  people from being criminalized but its  founder says it's not a long-term  solution i'm actually running an  organisation that i wish didn't have to  exist  um  i really want there to be better access  to medicinal cannabis at  a good price with really good quality  for patients in the uk at the moment  that isn't going to happen easily in the  meantime can card continues to help in  the policing of cannabis the important  bit from a police in perspective is we  don't want to criminalise people we  shouldn't be criminalising yes we need  to enforce the law around the possession  of cannabis because it's illegal but we  ultimately want to make sure that  individuals can access mississippi  cannabis where clearly there is a health  need  having experienced decades filled with  challenges andrew hopes the barriers  that he and so many others continue to  face around medicinal cannabis will be  broken down sooner rather than later  aisha zarhidsky news
 

